18557871,2026-01-08,Checking or savings account,Checking account,Managing an account,Deposits and withdrawals,"I am filing a complaint regarding improper handling of deposits, account restriction, and missing funds. 

I deposited a check that was legitimately endorsed to me by the named payee. The bank initially credited the deposit, but immediately placed a restriction on my account and denied me access to the funds. I was instructed to provide additional information in order to make the account good, which I attempted to do. 

Despite denying me access to the funds, the bank internally applied the deposited funds to cover a prior returned deposit. Later, the bank reversed the deposit entirely, debited the remaining balance in my account, and closed the account, stating that I was not the intended payee. At no point did I receive the benefit of the deposited funds, yet the bank used them to offset its own losses. 

Additionally, while my account was restricted, my employer direct deposit ( wages ) was deposited into the account. I was never given access to these wages and was never notified whether the funds were returned to my employer, applied to an alleged debt, or placed in a holding account. To this day, I have not received an accounting of what happened to my direct deposit.

I am requesting : 1. A full written accounting of all deposits, reversals, holds, and internal offsets 2. Written confirmation of the disposition of my employer direct deposit 3. Return of any funds improperly applied or withheld 4. Confirmation of whether this account was reported toXX/XX/XXXX or any other consumer reporting agency The banks actions denied me access to my own wages, lacked transparency, and resulted in account closure without proper disclosure.",,KEYCORP,WA,98188,,Web,2026-01-08,Closed with explanation,Yes
