18961742,2026-01-23,Student loan,Federal student loan servicing,Incorrect information on your report,Account status incorrect,"Company : Nelnet Product : Student Loan Issue : Incorrect information on credit report / Loan servicing transfer Complaint Description I am submitting this complaint regarding inaccurate delinquency reporting following a student loan servicing transfer from Great Lakes to Nelnet. 

My student loans were originally serviced by Great Lakes. At some point, servicing was transferred to Nelnet. I did not receive clear, timely, or adequate notice of this transfer. 
When I began receiving communications from Nelnet requesting payment, I was uncertain whether the contact was legitimate due to the prevalence of student loan fraud and scams. 

Because of this lack of clear notice and concerns about legitimacy, my payments were delayed while I attempted to verify whether Nelnet was the authorized servicer of my loans. As a result, Nelnet reported multiple 30-day and 60-day late payments to the credit bureaus.

Once the servicing transfer was confirmed as legitimate, I took immediate action to resolve the account. The delinquencies were not the result of unwillingness to pay, but rather confusion and uncertainty caused by the servicing transfer and insufficient communication.

I am currently seeing approximately eight 30-day late marks and eight 60-day late marks reported on my credit file as a result of this issue.

I am requesting the Nelnet review the service transfer, notification process, and payment history and correct or remove the delinquency reporting associated with this period, as it does not accurately reflect my intent or ability to repay and was caused by servicing transfer issues outside of my control.

I am seeking correction of my credit reporting to reflect the circumstances surrounding the transfer and lack of proper notice.",,"Nelnet, Inc.",MI,496XX,,Web,2026-01-23,Closed with explanation,Yes
